      },
      "message": "fix(app): refusals say what a setup owns in plain words, not \"furniture\"\n\nFive user-visible refusals (repair, update, setup name, reserved names\nfor setups and tools) said \"furniture\", our in-code word. They now name\nthe setup's stock, work offsets or fixtures. Same conditions, same\ncommands; a guard test keeps the word out of these refusals.\n\nFixes #878\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
