        "date": "2026-11-11T19:56:31Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): refusals say what a setup owns in plain words, not \"furniture\"\n\nReview round on #886: the \"not a model\" refusals fire for tools,\noperations, setups and program entries too, so \"part of a setup\" was\nfalse there. They now say \"is not a model - it is a setup's stock or\nwork offset, a setup, a tool, an operation or other CAM data\"; the\nfixture tag refusal uses the same condition and sentence. New test\nchecks a tool and an operation through RepairModel and UpdateModel.\n\nFixes #878\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
